= Writing Use Case Items

A `use_case` item describes a user goal in Karl Wiegers tabular form.

== Item template

[source,asciidoc]
----
[#UC-NNN, item, role=use_case, title="<Verb> <Object>"]
--
|===
| Actor | <who performs the workflow>
| Goal | <the complete user goal>
| Preconditions | <testable starting state>
| Postconditions | <measurable outcome>
| Main flow | 1. <step>
| Alternate flows | 1a. <error path the system handles>
|===

traceability:links[]
--
----

== Writing rules

* One complete user goal per use case, not a tool invocation.
* Preconditions must be testable states ("the extension is installed"), not opinions.
* Postconditions must be measurable ("the graph contains the new item"), not "coverage improves".
* Alternate flows cover error scenarios the system handles.

== Quality checklist

* Actor scope — names who performs the workflow.
* Goal scope — a complete goal, not a step.
* Testable preconditions and measurable postconditions.
* Alternate flows present for error cases.
